# Logging Discipline

Every `Debug.Log` allocates (message string, stack trace capture) and stalls — in WebGL it also marshals to the browser console. Logs are for **events**, never for **frames**.

## No logging in per-frame code

`Update`/`FixedUpdate`/`LateUpdate`, per-frame coroutine bodies, and per-message handlers that fire many times a second do not log. Not even "temporarily".

## Verbose logs are compiled out, including their string

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — string is built and allocated even if the log is filtered out
Debug.Log($"[Sim] tick {frame} units={units.Count}");

// ✅ GOOD — call and argument evaluation removed entirely in release
[System.Diagnostics.Conditional("ENABLE_VERBOSE_LOGS")]
private static void LogVerbose(string message)
{
    Debug.Log(message);
}

LogVerbose($"[Sim] tick {frame} units={units.Count}");
```

`Conditional` removes the call **including argument evaluation** — the interpolated string is never built when the symbol is off. A runtime `if (_verbose)` check does not do that.

## Errors and warnings stay, with context

Genuine failure paths follow the fail-fast rule: `Debug.LogError` / `LogWarning` with `[ClassName] MethodName — reason (id=…, state=…)`. Never a bare `Debug.LogError("error")`, never `catch { }`.

| Level | When |
|-------|------|
| **Error** | Required for this code path; skipping means wrong state, lost event, broken feature |
| **Warning** | Unexpected but recoverable, or possibly optional |
| **Log** | Rare lifecycle events (session start, reconnect, scene change) — never per frame |

## Agent checklist

- [ ] No `Debug.Log*` in `Update`/`FixedUpdate`/`LateUpdate`/coroutine loops/hot handlers
- [ ] Verbose/diagnostic logs go through a `[Conditional]` method, not a runtime flag
- [ ] Error/warning logs carry `[ClassName] Method — reason` and useful ids
- [ ] No silent `catch { }`
